Package: @PKG_NAME@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Depends: @SHLIBS_DEPENDS@
Suggests: @PKG_NAME@-dbgsym
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.sourceware.org/gdb/
Description: GNU Debugger @GDB_VERSION@ for @DIST_PRETTY@, installed in @PREFIX@
 GDB @GDB_VERSION@ with Python, TUI, XML target descriptions and LZMA
 mini-debuginfo support, built on @DIST_PRETTY@ and installed into
 @PREFIX@. It fully understands DWARF 5, which current GCC versions emit by
 default. The system gdb is left untouched.
 .
 Call it as @PREFIX@/bin/gdb, or put @PREFIX@/bin on PATH. Separate debug
 info is looked up in /usr/lib/debug, and auto-load scripts such as the
 libstdc++ pretty-printers of every gcc-N-opt package are loaded from
 /usr/share/gdb/auto-load.
